{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\8th\\8th MAths\\JPG\\013.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Introduction", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[82, 92], [177, 87], [178, 107], [84, 112]]}, {"text": "Wehavelearntaboutrationalnumbers,theirrepresentationonanumberline", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[100, 118], [528, 93], [529, 112], [101, 138]]}, {"text": "comparisonand alsoabouttheirproperties.Nowwewillearnaboutthereal", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[98, 138], [522, 111], [523, 130], [100, 157]]}, {"text": "numbers(rationalandirrational.theirpropertiesandrepresentationonanumber", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[98, 153], [552, 129], [553, 149], [99, 173]]}, {"text": "linebutbforeitlet'searnaboutthetyesofcimalnumbrswhichwillhepus", "conf": 0.734, "box": [[95, 169], [555, 148], [556, 170], [96, 191]]}, {"text": "understanding theconceptof irrationalnumbers.", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[95, 190], [368, 178], [369, 196], [96, 209]]}, {"text": "2.1Types ofDecimal Numbers", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[196, 221], [443, 210], [444, 232], [197, 244]]}, {"text": "There are two types of decimal numbers.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[66, 255], [293, 249], [293, 268], [66, 275]]}, {"text": "a)Terminating Decimal Numbers", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[64, 275], [251, 270], [251, 287], [65, 291]]}, {"text": "b) Non-Terminating Decimal Numbers", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[290, 269], [507, 259], [507, 276], [291, 286]]}, {"text": "a)Terminating Decimal Numbers", "conf": 0.86, "box": [[63, 292], [261, 288], [261, 304], [63, 309]]}, {"text": "When converting a fraction to a decimal by division method wemostly notice that the", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[61, 310], [546, 296], [547, 315], [61, 329]]}, {"text": "division is complete after certain steps and we get the remainder zero. In such cases, the", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[61, 328], [560, 315], [560, 335], [61, 347]]}, {"text": "quotient obtained as the decimal is called the terminating decimal.", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[61, 347], [437, 337], [437, 356], [61, 366]]}, {"text": "So, the terminating decimal numbers are those decimal numbers that have a finite", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[59, 365], [524, 354], [524, 373], [60, 384]]}, {"text": "number of digits after the decimal point. Let's consider a few examples.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[59, 384], [461, 376], [461, 392], [60, 401]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.859, "box": [[58, 413], [127, 411], [127, 429], [59, 431]]}, {"text": "43", "conf": 0.517, "box": [[107, 427], [126, 427], [126, 440], [107, 440]]}, {"text": "Express", "conf": 0.836, "box": [[59, 432], [114, 432], [114, 449], [59, 449]]}, {"text": "as a decimal number.", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[130, 431], [255, 427], [255, 444], [130, 448]]}, {"text": "Solution:", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[58, 450], [119, 448], [120, 466], [58, 468]]}, {"text": ".First divide the dividend 43 by the divisor 5. 5 goes into 43", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[59, 476], [403, 470], [404, 488], [60, 494]]}, {"text": "8.6", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[472, 480], [495, 480], [495, 498], [472, 498]]}, {"text": "eight times with 3 leftover. i.e. 5 × 8 = 40 r3", "conf": 0.851, "box": [[74, 495], [325, 491], [325, 508], [74, 512]]}, {"text": "43.0", "conf": 0.798, "box": [[464, 499], [495, 499], [495, 517], [464, 517]]}, {"text": ":Now the remainder 3 is less than the divisor 5. So, put a", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[59, 515], [388, 509], [388, 525], [60, 531]]}, {"text": "40", "conf": 0.61, "box": [[461, 518], [490, 516], [492, 535], [462, 538]]}, {"text": "decimal point after 8 in the quotient. Also put a decimal point", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[74, 533], [423, 528], [423, 545], [74, 550]]}, {"text": "30", "conf": 0.664, "box": [[474, 535], [495, 535], [495, 554], [474, 554]]}, {"text": "after the dividend43 and write an additional zero after it. So, 43", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[73, 552], [422, 546], [422, 563], [73, 569]]}, {"text": "-30", "conf": 0.652, "box": [[463, 554], [494, 551], [497, 573], [466, 576]]}, {"text": "will be written as 43.0 (43 is same as 43.0). The decimal point in", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[73, 571], [428, 566], [429, 582], [73, 587]]}, {"text": "the quotient and dividend must be aligned.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[73, 589], [317, 586], [317, 603], [73, 606]]}, {"text": ":Bring down the 0. The remainder 3will become30.", "conf": 0.859, "box": [[59, 608], [358, 605], [358, 622], [59, 625]]}, {"text": ".5 goes into 30 six times, so the quotient is 8.6 with zero remainder now.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[59, 629], [479, 624], [479, 642], [59, 647]]}, {"text": ".The division process ends here.", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[61, 648], [247, 648], [247, 664], [61, 664]]}, {"text": "Few more examples of terminating decimals include:", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[60, 695], [352, 694], [352, 711], [60, 712]]}, {"text": "=0.5寸=0.25,号=2.5,号=13.5", "conf": 0.773, "box": [[69, 718], [301, 718], [301, 745], [69, 745]]}, {"text": "NOTLFORSALE", "conf": 0.723, "box": [[69, 769], [160, 767], [161, 783], [69, 785]]}]}